  "notes": "TC-1 — Two-story aligned stack (hand check)\nINTENT: check the base path end to end: story shear build-up, capacity distribution, nailing, gravity statics, every ASD combo, accumulation of T/C at aligned wall ends, hardware, and the line equilibrium checks (G1–G12). Loads over the 10 ft gap between walls have nothing below: they are \"not carried\" (audit note) and must appear as excluded in G4 / G8.\nINPUTS: SDS 1.0, rho 1.0, seismic. Roof story ftf 9 ft, Level 1 ftf 10 ft. Line A 30 ft. Walls 10 ft at x = 0 and x = 20 on both stories (aligned). Wall DL 12 psf. Lateral 1.0E: Roof 4 k, Level 1 6 k. Gravity at Roof: full line D 150 / Lr 100 plf. At Level 1: full line D 120 / L 200 plf.\nHAND CALC:\n1. Story shear: V_roof = 4 k; V_1 = 4 + 6 = 10 k. Equal walls → 2.0 k (top) and 5.0 k (bottom) each.\n2. Unit shear: top v = 0.7·1.0·2000/10 = 140 plf → 6\" o.c. (312), D/C 0.45. Bottom v = 0.7·5000/10 = 350 plf > 312 → 4\" o.c. (470), D/C 0.74.\n3. Top wall gravity: D = 150·10/1000 + 12·10·9/1000 = 1.50 + 1.08 = 2.58 k → R = 1.29 k each end; Lr = 1.0 k → 0.5 each end.\n4. Top OTM(1.0E) = 2.0·9 = 18 k·ft → ±1.80 k.\n   Uplift (0.6−0.14SDS)D + 0.7E: 0.46·1.29 − 0.7·1.80 = −0.67 → T = 0.67 k (strap MSTC28 1535 lb).\n   Compression (1+0.14SDS)D + 0.7E: 1.14·1.29 + 1.26 = 2.73 k (governs over D+Lr 1.79 k and combo (6) 2.37 k).\n5. Bottom wall own gravity: D = 120·10/1000 + 12·10·10/1000 = 2.40 k → 1.20 each end; L = 2.0 k → 1.0 each end. OTM = 5·10 = 50 k·ft → ±5.00 k.\n6. Accumulated (own + wall above, same combo) at the base:\n   T: 0.46·1.20 − 3.50 = −2.95; + (−0.67) = −3.62 → T = 3.62 k → HDUE3 (3790 lb), D/C 0.96.\n   C: 1.14·1.20 + 3.50 = 4.87; + 2.73 = 7.60 k (governs over combo (6): 1.105·1.2 + 0.75·1.0 + 2.625 + 2.37 = 7.07 k).\n7. Line checks: G9 base moment Σ V·h = 4·9 + 10·10 = 136 k·ft. G8 1.0D: applied = 4.50 + 2.16 (roof + top walls) + 3.60 + 2.40 (L1 + bottom walls) = 12.66 k = foundation 9.96 + excluded (gap loads) 1.50 + 1.20 = 2.70 k.\nNOT HAND-CHECKED HERE: end posts are auto-sized by the NDS column check (SW-3 / SW-4: 6x4 for C = 7.60 k at 10 ft).\nWHERE TO LOOK: N-S / Line A → Checks tab (all OK), Walls → Detailed (SW-3 Σ end forces), Load path tab.",
